    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 18px;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
  }
  .kpi-label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .kpi-value {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .kpi-delta {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  section {
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 22px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
  }
  section h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    padding-bottom: 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  section h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin: 18px 0 10px;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  p, li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .chart-wrap {
    position: relative;
    height: 320px;
    margin: 14px 0 18px;
  }
  .chart-wrap.large {
    height: 400px;
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 10px 0 16px;
  }
  th, td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 10px 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  th {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }
  tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .highlight { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
  .good { color: var(--accent2); font-weight: 600; }
  .warn { color: var(--accent3); font-weight: 600; }
  .bad { color: var(--accent4); font-weight: 600; }
  .two-col {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 18px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .kpi-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }
  .note {
    background: #f0f9ff;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
    padding: 12px 14px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 12px 0;
  }
  ul.compact { margin: 8px 0; padding-left: 18px; }
  ul.compact li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
<header>
  <h1>Air Jordan Sneaker Resale Market Analysis</h1>
  <p>5,000 secondary-market transactions &nbsp;|&nbsp; January 2023 – September 2025 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Data-driven insights for sourcing and pricing strategy</p>
</header>
'''

# KPI cards
kpis = data['kpis']
html += f'''
<div class="kpi-grid">
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-label">Average Profit Margin</div>
    <div class="kpi-value">${kpis['avg_profit_margin']:,.2f}</div>
    <div class="kpi-delta">Median: ${kpis['median_profit_margin']:,.2f}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-label">Resale Premium Rate</div>
    <div class="kpi-value">{kpis['premium_rate']:.2f}%</div>
    <div class="kpi-delta">{kpis['negative_margin_pct']:.1f}% of transactions below retail</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-label">Average Days in Inventory</div>
    <div class="kpi-value">{kpis['avg_days_inventory']:.1f}</div>
    <div class="kpi-delta">Median: 14 days</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-label">Resale-to-Retail Ratio</div>
    <div class="kpi-value">{kpis['avg_resale_retail_ratio']:.3f}x</div>
    <div class="kpi-delta">Avg resale ${kpis['avg_resale']:,.2f} vs retail ${kpis['avg_retail']:,.2f}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-label">Top Colorway Margin</div>
    <div class="kpi-value">${kpis['top_colorway_margin']:,.2f}</div>
    <div class="kpi-delta">{kpis['top_colorway']}</div>
  </div>
</div>
'''

# Section 1: Market Overview
html += '''
<section id="market-overview">
  <h2>Market Overview & Transaction Summary</h2>
  <p>The dataset comprises <strong>5,000 transactions</strong> spanning <strong>January 2023 to September 2025</strong>. On average, sneakers resell at <strong>$273.23</strong> against an average retail of <strong>$191.17</strong>, yielding a mean profit margin of <strong>$82.06</strong> and a resale-to-retail multiplier of <strong>1.427x</strong>. However, the median margin is only <strong>$35.27</strong>, signaling a right-skewed distribution where a minority of high-premium sales lift the mean.</p>
  <p>Approximately <strong>61.3%</strong> of all transactions clear above retail, while <strong>38.7%</strong> sell at a loss relative to MSRP. The margin distribution is polarized: <strong>20.9%</strong> of sales generate margins above $200, and <strong>18.9%</strong> lose more than $50.</p>
  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <canvas id="marginDistChart"></canvas>
  </div>
  <p class="muted">Figure 1: Distribution of profit margins across all 5,000 transactions. The bimodal pattern reflects the strong condition effect—Deadstock sales cluster in the high-margin tail, while Used sales dominate the loss segment.</p>
</section>
'''

# Section 2: Model & Colorway Analysis
html += '''
<section id="model-colorway-analysis">
  <h2>Performance by Shoe Model & Colorway</h2>
  <h3>Model Rankings</h3>
  <p>Five silhouettes are represented, with <strong>Air Jordan 11 Retro</strong> leading on margin ($99.84 avg) despite the highest average retail ($227.48). <strong>Air Jordan 4 Retro</strong> follows closely at $95.76, while <strong>Air Jordan 1 Low</strong> trails at $50.52—roughly half the margin of the top tier. Volume is evenly distributed (18.5%–20.9% per model), so concentration risk is low.</p>
  <div class="two-col">
    <div>
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="modelMarginChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="modelDaysChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Model</th><th class="num">Transactions</th><th class="num">Avg Retail</th><th class="num">Avg Resale</th><th class="num">Avg Margin</th><th class="num">Premium Rate</th><th class="num">Avg Days</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
'''
for row in data['model_stats']:
    html += f'''<tr><td>{row['Shoe_Model']}</td><td class="num">{row['Transactions']:,}</td><td class="num">${row['Avg_Retail']:,.2f}</td><td class="num">${row['Avg_Resale']:,.2f}</td><td class="num">${row['Avg_Margin']:,.2f}</td><td class="num">{row['Premium_Rate']:.1f}%</td><td class="num">{row['Avg_Days']:.1f}</td></tr>\n'''
html += '''
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Colorway Rankings</h3>
  <p>Nine colorways appear, with <strong>Pine Green</strong> ($89.23 avg margin) and <strong>Military Blue</strong> ($87.55) forming the top tier. <strong>Black Cat</strong> sits at the bottom ($69.34), a gap of <strong>$19.89</strong> from Pine Green. Volume is balanced (10.7%–11.7% each), so no single colorway dominates liquidity.</p>
  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <canvas id="colorwayChart"></canvas>
  </div>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Colorway</th><th class="num">Transactions</th><th class="num">Avg Retail</th><th class="num">Avg Resale</th><th class="num">Avg Margin</th><th class="num">Premium Rate</th><th class="num">Avg Days</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
'''
for row in data['colorway_stats']:
    html += f'''<tr><td>{row['Colorway']}</td><td class="num">{row['Transactions']:,}</td><td class="num">${row['Avg_Retail']:,.2f}</td><td class="num">${row['Avg_Resale']:,.2f}</td><td class="num">${row['Avg_Margin']:,.2f}</td><td class="num">{row['Premium_Rate']:.1f}%</td><td class="num">{row['Avg_Days']:.1f}</td></tr>\n'''
html += '''
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>
'''

# Section 3: Condition Impact
html += '''
<section id="condition-impact">
  <h2>Impact of Shoe Condition on Resale Value</h2>
  <p>Condition is the single strongest pricing lever in the dataset. <strong>Deadstock (Brand New)</strong> items average <strong>$455.51</strong> in resale—<strong>$225.67</strong> above VNDS and <strong>$323.38</strong> above Used. Every Deadstock transaction in the dataset cleared above retail (100% premium rate), while no Used transaction did (0%). VNDS sits in the middle with an <strong>83.3%</strong> premium rate and a $37.62 average margin.</p>
  <div class="two-col">
    <div>
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="conditionResaleChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="conditionMarginChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Condition</th><th class="num">Transactions</th><th class="num">Avg Retail</th><th class="num">Avg Resale</th><th class="num">Avg Margin</th><th class="num">Premium Rate</th><th class="num">Avg Days</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
'''
for row in data['condition_stats']:
    html += f'''<tr><td>{row['Condition']}</td><td class="num">{row['Transactions']:,}</td><td class="num">${row['Avg_Retail']:,.2f}</td><td class="num">${row['Avg_Resale']:,.2f}</td><td class="num">${row['Avg_Margin']:,.2f}</td><td class="num">{row['Premium_Rate']:.1f}%</td><td class="num">{row['Avg_Days']:.1f}</td></tr>\n'''
html += '''
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="note">
    <strong>Sourcing implication:</strong> The $225.67 spread between Deadstock and VNDS far exceeds the $97.71 VNDS-to-Used gap. If capital allows, prioritize Deadstock inventory—its 100% above-retail clearance rate and $264.01 average margin offer the highest risk-adjusted return.
  </div>
  <h3>Model × Condition Margin Matrix</h3>
  <p>The condition premium is consistent across all five models. Air Jordan 11 Retro Deadstock commands the highest absolute margin ($311.64), while Air Jordan 1 Low Deadstock offers the lowest ($168.85)—still nearly 3× the Air Jordan 1 Low VNDS margin.</p>
  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <canvas id="modelCondHeatmap"></canvas>
  </div>
</section>
'''

# Section 4: Channel Performance & Inventory Velocity
html += '''
<section id="channel-performance">
  <h2>Sales Channel Performance & Inventory Velocity</h2>
  <p>The core strategic tension in resale is <strong>margin versus turnover speed</strong>. The data reveals a clear bifurcation:</p>
  <ul class="compact">
    <li><strong>High-velocity platforms (GOAT, StockX):</strong> Median time-to-sale of <strong>8 days</strong>, with 100% of inventory moving within 14 days. However, margins are compressed—StockX averages $73.92, the lowest of any channel.</li>
    <li><strong>High-margin platforms (Walk-in Retail, Stadium Goods, kick hub 2026):</strong> Median hold times of <strong>33–34 days</strong>, with fewer than 19% of sales closing inside two weeks. Walk-in Retail leads on margin ($89.55), but inventory sits 4.4× longer than on GOAT.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="two-col">
    <div>
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="channelMarginChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="channelDaysChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Channel</th><th class="num">Transactions</th><th class="num">Avg Resale</th><th class="num">Avg Margin</th><th class="num">Avg Days</th><th class="num">Median Days</th><th class="num">≤14 Days</th><th class="num">Premium Rate</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
'''
for row in data['channel_stats']:
    html += f'''<tr><td>{row['Sales_Channel']}</td><td class="num">{row['Transactions']:,}</td><td class="num">${row['Avg_Resale']:,.2f}</td><td class="num">${row['Avg_Margin']:,.2f}</td><td class="num">{row['Avg_Days']:.1f}</td><td class="num">{row['Median_Days']:.1f}</td><td class="num">{row['Pct_Fast']:.1f}%</td><td class="num">{row['Premium_Rate']:.1f}%</td></tr>\n'''
html += '''
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="note">
    <strong>Velocity insight:</strong> GOAT and StockX operate as near-instant liquidity providers. For resellers holding depreciating inventory (especially Used or slow colorways), these platforms minimize carrying-cost risk. For premium Deadstock pairs with strong colorway demand, Walk-in Retail or Stadium Goods can capture an extra $6–$16 per sale—provided the 25+ day hold is acceptable.
  </div>
  <h3>Condition × Channel Interaction</h3>
  <p>The condition premium is remarkably stable across channels. Deadstock margins range from $246.01 (StockX) to $274.73 (GOAT)—a spread of only $28.72. Used losses are similarly tight (-$59.84 to -$56.17). This suggests condition pricing is largely commoditized; the real channel decision is about <em>speed</em>, not <em>price discovery</em>.</p>
  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <canvas id="channelCondMarginChart"></canvas>
  </div>
</section>
'''

# Section 5: Temporal Trends
html += '''
<section id="time-trends">
  <h2>Temporal Trends & Seasonality</h2>
